      "role": "user",
      "content": "Can you explain the difference between high-glycemic index foods and low-glycemic index foods? specifically how they impact insulin response and blood sugar spikes.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "High-glycemic index (GI) foods are quickly digested, causing a rapid surge in blood sugar, which forces your pancreas to release a large amount of insulin. Low-GI foods, on the other hand, are digested slowly, leading to a more gradual rise in blood sugar and a gentler insulin response. This difference is crucial, as constant, sharp spikes in blood sugar and insulin are not ideal for metabolic health. Choosing low-GI options helps maintain more stable energy levels throughout the day.",
      "source": "target",
